1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,000
People's goals and barriers change week to week.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
Generic reminders don't show what they know about you, or why they suggest something.

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:16,600
A synthetic check-in starts as one plain sentence.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,600
It proposes 3 values, each with the words it came from. Mood gave none.

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:26,100
Sleep is corrected to 6.5 hours; the other two are confirmed.

6
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,200
Nothing is saved until the review is submitted.

7
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:34,110
Saved values update the Health Clone Passport.

8
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:39,110
The evidence thread traces one value from the check-in to the card.

9
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:43,310
A card with no value in 14 days is withheld, not guessed.

10
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:47,230
After a pain report, the next step routes to a person.

11
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:50,630
The person can choose, defer or ask a professional.

12
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:54,990
Crisis language is not processed.

13
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:59,190
A fixed hand-off points to a person. Nothing is saved.

14
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:04,070
Real health data is switched off in this build.

15
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:08,570
The server refuses the request: 12 of 12 governance gates are open.

16
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,600
The timeline shows what each saved check-in changed.

17
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:19,490
The learning lab reads committed training and evaluation runs.

18
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:24,490
Each number carries its run ID, split, seed and failure count.

19
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:30,420
On 141 held-out synthetic prompts, the base model passed 45.

20
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:35,420
Both fine-tuned stages passed all 141. 90 base replies were empty.

21
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:40,220
These are simulated results, not patient outcomes.

22
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:46,320
The research console shows the live loop, then the offline training stages.

23
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:53,200
Live: check-in, safety checks, proposals, review, memory, passport.

24
00:01:53,200 --> 00:02:00,000
Offline: synthetic members, evaluation, fine-tuning, frozen comparison.

25
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:06,800
Synthetic data only. No diagnosis, treatment or dosing. No clinical review.

26
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:13,600
The rules caught 74 of 74 test violations: a measurement, not a proof.

27
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:19,400
It runs today as a hosted prototype.

28
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:25,200
Reaching people needs consent, privacy, clinical oversight and a study first.

29
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:31,000
Next: a clinical reviewer, a consented pilot and a pre-registered measure.

30
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The prototype link is in the submission.
